    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0317" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/5–2648:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-26T18:00:00-04:00">May 26, 1948—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1812. Personal for Caffery. Re French
                    suggested debate of German program by Assembly Foreign Affairs Committee
                        (Douglas’ 232 to you<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d188-f1"/>) we can conceive of nothing that would more effectively
                    destroy basis of conference if such debate took place before agreement at London
                    and we assume French will have perception to abandon any such idea. Pls advise
                    to what extent London agreement if reached will require Assembly approval before
                    announcement of final French Govt approval and your estimate of effect such
                    debate, if any, on implementation of program.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London as Deptel 1924.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="1" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 2271, Delsec 1754, May 25,
                    from London, <ref target="#pg280">p. 280</ref>.</p>
            </note>
